From c3151ade979a9fbc9963c032f8bdc8ce1aa56782 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:36:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: render into a decoder's own buffer when it asks
 for more than the picture

A decoder can ask for a frame larger than its picture: the Dirac decoder asks
for an edge around it and moves the planes inside. The picture lent for
direct rendering, made for the output format, was checked against that size
by assertions alone; in a build without them the decoder wrote past the
picture's planes into the next ones, and the picture shown, its planes not
moved, was off by the edge. A Dirac video showed coloured pictures and a
misshapen frame.

Give such a decoder its own buffer, as for a picture not aligned for it,
and copy its pictures out.
---
 modules/codec/avcodec/video.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c b/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c
index 971748c..ae55ffd 100644
--- a/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c
+++ b/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c
@@ -1626,9 +1626,17 @@ static int lavc_dr_GetFrame(struct AVCodecContext *ctx, AVFrame *frame,
 
     avcodec_align_dimensions2(ctx, &width, &height, aligns);
 
-    /* Check that the picture is suitable for libavcodec */
-    assert(pic->p[0].i_pitch >= width * pic->p[0].i_pixel_pitch);
-    assert(pic->p[0].i_lines >= height);
+    /* Check that the picture is suitable for libavcodec. A decoder can ask for
+     * more than its picture: the Dirac decoder asks for an edge around it and
+     * moves the planes inside. A picture of the output format cannot hold it. */
+    if (pic->p[0].i_pitch < width * pic->p[0].i_pixel_pitch ||
+        pic->p[0].i_lines < height)
+    {
+        if (!atomic_exchange(&sys->b_dr_failure, true))
+            msg_Warn(dec, "%dx%d asked for, larger than the picture: "
+                     "disabling direct rendering", width, height);
+        goto error;
+    }
 
     for (int i = 0; i < pic->i_planes; i++)
     {
